    "problem_statement": "Jobs with `until()` not being cancelled when they should be\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using the `until()` method to set a cancellation time for scheduled jobs, the jobs are not being cancelled at the expected time. Instead, they continue running past their intended cancellation deadline.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport schedule\nimport datetime\n\ndef my_job():\n    print(\"Job executed\")\n\n# Schedule a job to run every 5 seconds until 11:35:20\nwith mock_datetime(2020, 1, 1, 11, 35, 10):\n    schedule.every(5).seconds.until(datetime.time(11, 35, 20)).do(my_job)\n    \n    # At 11:35:50, the job should have been cancelled already\n    with mock_datetime(2020, 1, 1, 11, 35, 50):\n        schedule.run_pending()\n        print(f\"Jobs remaining: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")  # Expected: 0, Actual: 1\n```\n\nThe job should be automatically cancelled when the current time reaches or exceeds the `until()` time, but it continues to exist in the scheduler."
